    <h1>Gravity: The Pressure Bulge</h1>
    <p class="lead">General relativity models gravity as a geometric depression in spacetime—a "well" that pulls objects inward. The Temporal Decoupling framework proposes an alternative mechanical ontology: matter creates an <strong>outward pressure bulge</strong> into the background medium. Objects are pushed inward by the surrounding TSC pressure differential.</p>

