    <h2>Inverted Causality, Identical Mathematics</h2>
    <p>This is not a challenge to the predictive power of general relativity. The pressure gradient generated by the bulge naturally recovers the standard Poisson equation (<code>∇²Φ = 4πGρ</code>) in the weak-field limit. The mathematics of orbital mechanics, lensing, and time dilation remain unchanged.</p>
    <p>What changes is the <strong>causal mechanism</strong>:</p>
    <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #334155;">
      <li><strong>Standard View:</strong> Spacetime curvature dictates how matter moves. (Geometry → Motion)</li>
      <li><strong>Decoupling View:</strong> Matter density displaces the background medium, and the resulting pressure differential dictates motion. (Density → Pressure → Motion)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Hydrodynamic Origin</h2>
    <p>When the timeline intersects a TSC entity, it creates hydrodynamic resistance. Dense accumulations of these intersections (planets, stars, galaxies) push outward against the static scalar medium. The surrounding TSC acts like a fluid trying to restore equilibrium. This inward-directed pressure is what we experience as gravitational attraction.</p>
    <p>This mechanical picture elegantly bridges the gap between quantum particle drag (micro-scale) and cosmic structure formation (macro-scale) using a single, unified fluid-dynamic principle.</p>

    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: #fff7ed; border-left: 4px solid #f97316; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #9a3412;">Why This Matters</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0; color: #7c2d12;">By treating gravity as a pressure differential rather than pure geometry, we open a direct pathway to unify gravitational mechanics with quantum hydrodynamics, without requiring extra dimensions or unobservable gravitons.</p>
